{
  "schema": "rain-fly-record/v2",
  "run_id": "FR-053afd4ca05528fee582ba29",
  "plan": {
    "schema": "rain-fly-plan/v2",
    "design": {
      "schema": "rain-fly-design/v3",
      "question": "[scripted] ECHO-01: does the fly's self-model let it walk where it intends after an impairment it is never told about?",
      "hypothesis": "[scripted] Without its self-model, the fly's walking strays further from its intended path after a hidden impairment, from held-out conditions, than with it.",
      "competing_hypothesis": "[scripted] The reduced-order controller's own feedback (turning back from edges, its tether) keeps its path as close to its intentions as a self-model would.",
      "parameters": {
        "seed_count": 9,
        "treatment": {
          "kind": "echo_impairment",
          "variant": "reactive"
        }
      },
      "analysis": {
        "method": "matched_seed_sign_test",
        "metric": "impaired_path_error",
        "expected_direction": "increase",
        "minimum_effect": 0.19
      },
      "budget": {
        "max_simulated_seconds": 16000
      },
      "provenance": {
        "generation": "scripted",
        "decision_sha256": null,
        "source_ids": [],
        "parent_record_sha256": null
      }
    },
    "ir": {
      "schema": "rain-scientific-experiment/v1",
      "domain": "fly-behavior-simulation",
      "backend": "digital-fly",
      "backend_version": "digital-fly-behavior/v3 (digital-fly/8 reduced-order-fsm/v1)",
      "question": "In the digital fly simulator, how does the ECHO controller with no self-model (the reduced-order controller alone) change mean path error of steady walking from the hidden impairment's onset to the end of the run, against the full ECHO self-model under the same hidden conditions on matched seeds?",
      "hypothesis": "The ECHO controller with no self-model (the reduced-order controller alone) will increase impaired_path_error by at least 0.19 fraction on average over 9 matched seeds drawn after preregistration, compared with the full ECHO self-model under the same hidden conditions, and an exact one-sided sign test on the seeds that differ will find the increase at alpha 0.05.",
      "observables": [
        {
          "id": "impaired_path_error",
          "unit": "fraction",
          "description": "mean path error of steady walking from the hidden impairment's onset to the end of the run"
        },
        {
          "id": "late_path_error",
          "unit": "fraction",
          "description": "mean path error of steady walking over the run's last 40 s"
        },
        {
          "id": "baseline_path_error",
          "unit": "fraction",
          "description": "mean path error of steady walking before the hidden impairment"
        },
        {
          "id": "detection_latency_s",
          "unit": "s",
          "description": "time from the hidden impairment's onset to the fly's first noticing that its predictions fail (undefined without a self-model or if never noticed)"
        },
        {
          "id": "attribution_latency_s",
          "unit": "s",
          "description": "time from the onset to the fly's first concluding that it changed itself (undefined without one)"
        },
        {
          "id": "identification_error",
          "unit": "fraction",
          "description": "relative error of the fly's final beliefs about the impaired gains and biases against the hidden values (undefined without a self-model)"
        },
        {
          "id": "false_alarms_per_min",
          "unit": "1/min",
          "description": "conclusions other than 'nothing changed' before the onset, per minute"
        },
        {
          "id": "impaired_walked_m",
          "unit": "m",
          "description": "distance walked after the onset"
        },
        {
          "id": "coverage_90",
          "unit": "fraction",
          "description": "share of observed self-motion components inside the fly's own predicted central 90% interval (0.9 is calibrated)"
        },
        {
          "id": "mean_paired_delta",
          "unit": "fraction",
          "description": "treatment minus control impaired_path_error, averaged over the seeds where both are defined"
        },
        {
          "id": "sign_test_p_expected",
          "unit": "probability",
          "description": "exact one-sided sign test p-value for a increase, over untied seeds"
        },
        {
          "id": "sign_test_p_opposite",
          "unit": "probability",
          "description": "the same test in the opposite direction"
        }
      ],
      "independent_variables": [
        "the ECHO controller with no self-model (the reduced-order controller alone)"
      ],
      "dependent_variables": [
        "impaired_path_error"
      ],
      "controls": [
        "baseline arm: the full ECHO self-model under the same hidden conditions",
        "matched seeds: each seed places the fly, draws its stimuli and seeds its random streams identically in both arms",
        "the seeds are drawn by the host after preregistration from SHA-256 of the registry receipt and a random nonce in the authorization, so neither the design nor the operator chooses them",
        "fixed apparatus settings, both arms — impairment block: groomHz = 0, takeoffHz = 0, walkStartHz = 1, walkStopHz = 0.1",
        "the fly's version, controller, full parameter table and source digest are bound into the plan digest"
      ],
      "parameter_constraints": [
        "11 closed protocols with host-built arenas, stimuli and hidden perturbation schedules",
        "controller configurations override model parameters only, within their ranges; FlyBody and published values are fixed",
        "the integration settings (physics, sensing and decision periods) are never varied",
        "at most 16000 simulated fly-seconds per experiment",
        "8-16 seeds, drawn by the host after preregistration",
        "a minimum effect at or above the host's 0.09 fraction for impaired_path_error"
      ],
      "resource_budget": {
        "execution_steps": 432000,
        "replay_steps": 432000,
        "max_samples": 18
      },
      "statistical_analysis": {
        "method": "Exact one-sided sign test on the untied matched seeds at alpha 0.05, with at least 6 untied seeds, and a mean paired difference beyond the minimum effect; frozen rain-criteria/v1",
        "independent_replicates": 9,
        "uncertainty": "The p-values are exact binomial tail probabilities over seeds of one deterministic model: they say how consistently the two arms differ across this simulator's seeds, not how uncertain anything is about a population, and nothing about real flies."
      },
      "falsification": {
        "metric": "sign_test_p_opposite",
        "op": "<=",
        "value": 0.05,
        "unit": "probability"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "generation": "scripted",
        "decision_sha256": null,
        "source_ids": [],
        "parent_record_sha256": null
      },
      "limitations": [
        "The digital fly's controller is a reduced-order state machine. It simulates no neurons; its links to Virtual Fly Brain terms are labels, not mechanisms.",
        "Model parameters were chosen for this simulator, not measured or fitted; a result describes the simulator with these values.",
        "Flight is kinematic: no aerodynamics and no MuJoCo physics run in these experiments.",
        "The arena is a box with primitive obstacles and a relative light proxy (not lux); odour, temperature, humidity, airflow and food are not simulated.",
        "Compensation is of abstract movement gains in the reduced-order simulator, not validated motor control; a strong impairment cannot be fully compensated within the body's 4 cm/s. Identification (the identification error) is measured apart from compensation (the path errors).",
        "The ECHO self-model is a computational model of the fly's own sensorimotor gains, built over the reduced-order body. Its compensation acts on abstract movement gains of that body; it is not validated biological motor control, and FlyBody's physics does not run.",
        "The perturbations are the experimenter's models of an impairment, a push, a turning surface, a sensor fault and an obstacle, applied by the simulator. The fly is never given their labels, causes or schedule; it meets only their consequences through its self-motion sense, its touch and its legs' stepping.",
        "The conditions are the held-out evaluation set, in an arena the self-model was not developed in; its constants were chosen on the development set alone and frozen before evaluation.",
        "A measurement of prediction, attribution or retention describes a functional self-model in a simulator. It is not evidence of awareness or subjective experience.",
        "Re-simulation is exact on the JavaScript engine that made a record; Math functions differ in their last bits between engines, so on another engine a record is reported as not re-simulable rather than checked.",
        "A result characterizes the simulator and is never empirical evidence about Drosophila."
      ]
    },
